{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.6776 acc, outperforming RNA-only config_002 (0.6501) by ~2.7%, confirming the image modality contributes meaningfully. However, we have no data on how a stronger image encoder (ViT-L vs ResNet50) affects performance. This experiment (config_008) is a clean single-variable change from config_001—only the image encoder upgrades from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l—while keeping scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted fusion, and multiprofile fixed. It directly tests whether a more expressive image representation (ViT-L, ~307M params vs ResNet50's ~25M) can amplify the multimodal advantage. This is the best next step because: (1) the image encoder is the largest untested design lever with the highest expected impact on accuracy; (2) it isolates one variable for clear attribution; (3) with 7 experiments remaining, establishing whether ViT-L helps now guides whether to invest in transformer aggregation or VIT-L-based configs later. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-high, roughly 8–10 GPU hours (ViT-L forward/backward is ~3–5× costlier than ResNet50, while the RNA pipeline is unchanged), so it is more expensive than config_001 but justified by the potential accuracy gain."
}

